3. United India Insurance Company has preferred Miscellaneous First Appeal No.104132 of 2017 challenging the impugned judgment and award on liability as well as quantum of compensation;
whereas the claimants have preferred MFA Crob No.100049 of 2018 seeking enhancement of compensation.
NC: 2023:KHC-D:11253-DB C/W MFA.CROB No. 100049 of 2018 4.

Our answer for the above points is as under:
Point No.1: in the negative;
Point No.2: partly in the affirmative; Point No.3: as per final order.

Judgment and award dated 28th March, 2017 passed in MVC No.605 of 2003 by the Principal Senior Civil Judge and CJM and Addl. MACT, Dharwad is modified by enhancing the compensation to Rs.7,85,958/- in lieu of Rs.6,79,398/- awarded by the Tribunal;
- 24 - NC: 2023:KHC-D:11253-DB C/W MFA.CROB No. 100049 of 2018 4. Enhanced compensation carries interest at the rate of 6% per annum from the date of petition till realisation;
5. Respondents 1 and 2 are jointly and severally be liable to pay the compensation;
6. Amount in deposit if any, shall be transferred to the Tribunal forthwith for onward disbursement to the claimants;
7. Registry to draw award accordingly.
8. Send back the Trial court records with copy of this judgment and award.
